>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. The crystal connection table depicts terminal sulfur and two CO ligands. In the optimized input, S1–C5 is 1.754 Å, C5–O6 is 1.202 Å, the corresponding published calculated bond orders are approximately 1.22 and 1.81; The other CO has a C–O distance of 1.171 Å. The input geometry supports an OCS limiting form with a covalent S–C bond. Localized 11 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Checked each ligand's bond orders and formal charges against the input geometry. The atom order and coordinates of all 55 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 52 nonmetal covalent bonds: 48 within range, 1 outside range and 3 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 6–7 C-O 1.2023 Å. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

>  <UPSTREAM_COMPARISON>
Equivalent

>  <SPIN_REVIEW>
Not independently verified

