>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. Both B atoms have two B–N bonds and the Ru–B bond from the same-ID CSD graph. Both optimized Ru–B distances are 2.052 Å, WBO 1.091, 1.092. Write the two anionic boryl X-type bonds as covalent Ru–B single bonds, Both B atoms are then neutral with three bonds, Adjust the metal formal charge for covalent electron counting. This prevents SDF sanitization from reassigning either B as a diradical. Localized 40 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 59 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 64 nonmetal covalent bonds: 56 within range, 0 outside range and 8 with sparse controls. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

